      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-41907",
      ":question/problem": "Two standard dice are rolled. Define $A$ to be the event \"the sum of the outcomes is a prime number.\" It is known that $P(A) = 0.42$ to $2$ decimal places. To two decimal places, what is the probability that the sum of the outcomes has more than $2$ divisors?"
